  "notes": "Per-level iceberg persistence: the hidden refill fires only while visible depth survives at the level. Measured: the gate works directionally \u2014 ice80_resid lifts empties 5.5x over the matched per-unit cell while pushing hidden share to 0.41 (2x tape) \u2014 but magnitudes stay ~2 orders off (1% vs 47%): even gated reload makes the touch refill almost surely across a burst. The residual sharpens to a *budget* mechanism: real iceberg reserves are finite \u2014 consumed once and gone \u2014 not a persistent refill channel, so level exhaustion on the tape is genuinely absorbing.",
